MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners and Duets II feel like natural next choices because paired voices and polished, melodic singing connect with what I enjoyed in A Musical Affair, Stages, and my vocal ensemble recordings.",
    "Glen Campbell: Greatest Hits fits the melodic country side of my listening reflected in Golden and 747, making it a plausible choice alongside my stronger interest in duets today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Same Trailer Different Park and In The Lonely Hour miss my current mood because country storytelling and intimate contemporary pop are less appealing to me now than sweeping voices and relaxing arrangements.",
    "25 and Oscd Ad Adele 21 have an appealing vocal focus, but a strong solo voice alone does not give me the paired singing or orchestral feel I would choose today. Title gives me too little evidence of either quality."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in vocal music seems to have been extended too broadly to contemporary solo pop, although the style of singing and accompaniment matters to my choice.",
    "Golden and 747 seem to have led to several country suggestions, while that part of my listening is only a secondary interest right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My Downton Abbey recordings and The Most Relaxing Classical Music in the Universe suggest that atmosphere and gentle orchestral arrangements deserve more attention.",
    "A Musical Affair, Amor & Pasion, and Stages point toward expressive, theatrical singing; that connection matters more to me today than simply finding another melodic album."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices recognize my interest in melodic singing and some country music, but only the duet albums closely capture my current preference for expressive voices and orchestral warmth."
}
